1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
How does VLA 2.0 on dual Orin-X, the distilled build, perform?

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:08,120
One night, PA and I are driving a MONA M03.

3
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:12,280
First, a look at the version number: dual Orin-X, distilled build. We set the nav simply.

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:18,040
I tried starting from standstill and it actually entered roaming — so in this basement car park...

5
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:24,600
...it just starts driving out. It can move off inside the car park, but we hadn't even set a route.

6
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:31,520
I set one. Let me say up front, this build is very, very early — ignore the SR display.

7
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:36,160
Just focus on how the dual Orin-X performs. It's so close to that car!

8
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:45,200
That gave me a fright. That counts as precise measurement — millimetre-level, right?

9
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:51,520
Climbing, the speed was 22 km/h; once on ground level it dropped to 16 km/h.

10
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:58,240
Millisecond-level, millisecond-level speed. It's heading over there — is that wrong? What's up with you? No, it's right.

11
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:05,840
Right — it precisely drove into the exit barrier, and the barrier lifts, out of the car park.

12
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:11,240
From the basement to the exit, the whole run shows the dual Orin-X capability isn't bad at all.

13
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:16,920
Damn, you had no exterior view outside — I'll fill it in for you. So this one's on me.

14
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:22,000
Originally we planned to let it stop so PA could open the equipment on the car roof.

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:28,560
But after it drove out we couldn't bear to interrupt, so we just let it keep driving. Starting with the model's basic capabilities...

16
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:33,480
Entering the familiar Mubei Road, we look at two scenarios that definitely would have meant hard braking before.

17
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:38,800
First, continuous oncoming traffic on a narrow road. We see the white car squeezing our space to get past a tricycle.

18
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:43,280
In that situation the model didn't slow much.

19
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:48,400
It only slowed slightly as a show of respect, and passed through the oncoming traffic very calmly.

20
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:54,760
That's their problem, that's their problem. Next is a ghost-probe pop-out scenario.

21
00:01:54,760 --> 00:02:00,560
Pushed onto the user — that state — honestly, you don't even need to say anything. Look, it's fine, it's fine, it's fine, it's fine.

22
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:05,640
The braking was decent. You're so tense. The braking was decent. I nearly burned up right here.

23
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:10,400
Although the model can handle it, I'd still urge them to optimise it.

24
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:16,000
The deceleration in similar scenarios should be a bit bigger, because a pedestrian's crossing path often...

25
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,680
...can't be predicted. You can see the distilled build on dual Orin-X...

26
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:26,440
...has a very high model ceiling. Its tolerance really is completely different from before.

27
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:31,280
That means many scenarios that used to need the safety fallback to solve...

28
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:36,440
...can now be resolved by the model's own capability. We said before that XOS 6.3.0's...

29
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:41,560
...biggest trait is reacting very fast — and dual Orin-X is actually a lot like it.

30
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:47,520
Still Mubei Road. You'll see there are queued cars ahead, and here the model...

31
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:53,800
...is preparing to overtake. Isn't this — has it got it wrong? Come back, come back, come back. Yeah, come back, come back.

32
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:58,920
Yeah, it flashed me twice. The small flaw is that its swing back isn't quite enough.

33
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:03,480
I think if it could keep a bit more right and leave a big gap, that would be even better.

34
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:09,360
Down here you can see the shadow of the intersection following and going-around we posted a few days ago.

35
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:14,240
There's a car temporarily stopped — not using this thing... look, look, look. Whoa.

36
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:21,760
This go-around is fast too, really fast. It's not just silky, it has to be fast, because everyone can do silky now.

37
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:27,360
The bar is high — silky and fast. And here we merge onto the main road.

38
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:30,160
In the opposite lane, vehicles are making quick U-turns.

39
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:41,200
It flashed, flashed, flashed. In space and scene understanding, the test build also shows strong ability.

40
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:46,280
XOS 6.3.0 drove this road too. There's construction on the right, so we're driving on the left.

41
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:52,080
Now you see oncoming traffic, and VLA 2.0 moves right to open up space.

42
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:58,160
Right after that, a big truck — we stay on the right, still creeping.

43
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:06,040
It feels like it could pull out at any moment. And when the Denza finishes, it's ready to pull off, then sees a car still far ahead.

44
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:13,640
It stopped completely. I don't get it. Damn, how do I put this long-temporal ability, guys?

45
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:22,040
Yeah, dual Orin-X long temporal — and there's more, still more cars.

46
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:26,240
Just watch whether it goes after the car ahead clears, and you'll know where the model's ability actually stands

47
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:33,240
Whether it goes or not, I won't judge — you guys tell me. This is a dual Orin-X car

48
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:45,720
And it keeps going — see that? It keeps going around and then gives the space back

49
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:49,720
I'll stop talking, I'll stop talking — just watch, this is the dual Orin-X capability, dual Orin-X

50
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:56,360
This is VLA — someone say something — this is the dual Orin-X capability, look

51
00:04:56,360 --> 00:05:02,560
OK, this is dual Orin-X. Look at this — this is the large model, this is AI

52
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:07,680
This is physical AI. Now there's an oncoming car again, so we do the same thing

53
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:13,840
Move right immediately, then complete the pass through this intersection. Its scene understanding really is very good

54
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:20,160
The order of who goes first, waiting when it should wait — it did all of it, and did it well

55
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:25,760
Near Guangzhou Honda, the meeting situation is similar — two lanes, someone parked, so we borrow the lane and go around

56
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:30,400
This one's impressive too — the moment it sees a car far ahead, it pulls over to the side right away

57
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:37,000
This stretch — here it comes, watch, duck aside a bit, then pull back out. See that?

58
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:42,280
It's the same as the car ahead. Once you've been through similar scenes many times, you start to wonder

59
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:47,000
Am I actually driving the Orin distilled build right now, or the three-Turing version?

60
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:52,200
Narrow-space passing ability — we can look at this scene. We're about to enter the right-turn-only lane

61
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:57,040
The straight lane has a long queue here, and on the right is the bike-lane railing

62
00:05:57,040 --> 00:06:03,080
So damn good — a narrow road like this, it can absolutely get through. Holy crap. Think about it, it wouldn't dare before

63
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:10,800
Back with VLA, when meeting a car it would sit there thinking. Oh man — don't give me that boilerplate, OK?

64
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:16,880
The features dual Orin-X keeps are the same — there's also efficiency. You can see it reads the car ahead slowing down

65
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:23,840
The distilled build watches for a while, then immediately changes lanes to overtake. See that?

66
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:28,400
Look at this lane change here — its handling is different from 630's. Same with this efficiency-driven choice

67
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:35,560
The bus slows down, the left side is fairly open, so it gives two quick flicks of the wheel and changes to the left lane fast

68
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:41,120
This going-around — holy crap, this efficiency-driven choice, choosing for efficiency is exhausting, because the bus is slow

69
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:46,440
So it's basically the same as wanting to overtake. Here we're in the U-turn lane

70
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:51,320
Queuing in the right lane, the distilled build follows for a while — but watch its following distance here

71
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:57,280
It leaves a big gap. It keeps thinking about whether it can change into the right lane — here it comes

72
00:06:57,280 --> 00:07:02,640
It realized, then dodged this whole queue, so it really did make that choice

73
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:16,120
Here it comes, this one's strong too, but you can tell the reaction really isn't as badass as 630's

74
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:20,360
But here — see that? It just goes straight around, comes straight around

75
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:24,920
And then it doesn't have to queue. So if dual Orin-X has this ability, isn't that pretty strong?

76
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:31,120
Right, although all three scenes above were efficiency-driven choices

77
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:36,760
It's actually still quite strong, actually still quite strong. So if dual Orin-X has this ability

78
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:42,920
Isn't that pretty strong? All three scenes are efficiency-oriented choices, but it's not hard to see

79
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:48,320
The gap between it and three-Turing. Three-Turing handles these scenes effortlessly

80
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:53,960
Dual Orin-X just isn't that decisive. A very important trait of XPeng's assisted driving

81
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:58,120
Is efficiency. I think the distilled build does pretty well in this respect

82
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:03,560
I just don't know how much of it the production version will keep. Another surprise this time

83
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:07,760
Is the pre-start ability at traffic lights. The distilled build's trigger rate here

84
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:11,840
Is especially high. You can see here — my god, there are still 4 seconds and it's already about to go

85
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:18,880
See that? There are still 4 seconds and it's already gone. These native VLA 2.0 abilities are right here

86
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:24,360
We'd wonder whether a scene like this is emergence again, but it happened more than once

87
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:31,600
Again — countdown at 3 seconds, and the distilled build moved off again. Wait, wait, wait — nice, nice

88
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:37,160
Emergence shows the model must have seen far too many similar scenes during pre-training

89
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:43,400
As long as you're the lead car at the lights, you can often trigger some of the distilled build's traits — including some of the highlights, all covered above

90
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:48,400
We really only drove for 2 hours, so its problems haven't been exposed all that much

91
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:51,000
There was one time the problem was a wrong lane selection.

92
00:08:55,000 --> 00:09:00,800
Anyone who's made it this far is likely delighted by the smoothness of the distilled build.

93
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:08,120
And its ceiling went beyond what many people expected. At the XOS 6.3.0 launch event,

94
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:16,160
Liu Xianming spent a whole minute on XPeng's distillation approach. He said XPeng's distillation isn't simple cutting,

95
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:21,880
not simply chopping parameter count — he wants to preserve the model's underlying capability as much as possible.

96
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:27,440
In distillation, XPeng also updated the encoding scheme to keep only the key information,

97
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:31,440
hugely compressing the token count, so the compute load drops right away.

98
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:39,600
Two-layer supervision makes sure important information isn't cut. From our early preview so far,

99
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:46,440
its pure model capability has been largely preserved. So what's the difference between three-Turing and the dual Orin-X distilled build?

100
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:52,080
In terms of pure model capability, in daily driving you often really won't feel much difference.

101
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:58,240
We also posted a video today asking you to guess which run was the dual Orin-X one.

102
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:02,920
I think the main difference is in the reaction. For example, here,

103
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:11,080
the dual Orin-X observes a bit longer before a lane change; three-Turing anticipates and reacts faster, more composed.

104
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:16,200
With this distilled version, you'll find its ceiling is very high.

105
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:20,280
Its smoothness, comfort and flexibility are all very obvious traits.

106
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:25,760
So I think if the production version keeps 80% of the capability,

107
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:34,640
I'd be satisfied. So that's everything from the early — early preview of the VLA 2.0 dual Orin-X distilled build.

108
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:38,160
I'm Rourou Babi, and that's it for this episode's video.

109
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,520
See you next time.

